       The ddlleerrrroorr() function returns a human‐readable, null‐terminated string
       describing  the  most  recent error that occurred from a call to one of
       the functions in the dlopen API since the last call to ddlleerrrroorr().   The
       returned string does _n_o_t include a trailing newline.

       ddlleerrrroorr()  returns NULL if no errors have occurred since initialization
       or since it was last called.

